  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday night through Thursday)\nIssued at 254 AM EDT Fri Aug 14 2026\n\nLittle change in the long-term forecast with a dominant ridge \ncentered over the Mississippi Valley region and amplifying over \nour region through the weekend. As such, expect a continuation of \nsummertime heat and humidity, with temperatures in the mid to \nupper 90s and dew points in the 70s over the CWA outside of the \nfar northeast mountains. The above normal temperatures will remain\nin place through the beginning of next week, with heat indices in\nthe 100-108 range reaching Heat Advisory criteria over most of \nour CWA through the first of next week. \n\nBy mid-week, the ridge begins to flatten and shifts westward over \nthe Southern Plains; however, this will not provide much relief from \nthe mid-August heat. Given precipitable water values of 1.5-2.1 \ninches and our area residing along the eastern periphery of the \nridge, the prospect for diurnal afternoon thunderstorms will \ncontinue into next week. Coverage will depend on whether any \ndisturbances propagate through the flow into our area. Therefore,\nthe details of just how convectively active the period will be \nshould come into better focus over the next couple of days.",
